title font5x7 diaeresis-accent vowels corpus -- the fifth lean, GREEN
prompt Read crux/REMEMBER.md and the road-ahead docs; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, one rota deep-read, send often. baton prin recur
think REMEMBER's live edge is the Season G open-media font family; the accented-Latin family now reads as two unifying fonts (font5x7_accented lowercase 21, font5x7_upper uppercase 21) with the tilde vowels the most recent lap. Walked the family for the next real gap rather than another small increment.
think Found a genuine gap crux-first: the accent-mark taxonomy has four leans drawn on vowels (acute right, grave left, circumflex centered peak, tilde wave) plus the German umlaut two-dot mark on a/o/u -- yet the same two-dot diaeresis mark spells other languages on OTHER vowels a German name never reaches: e diaeresis, i diaeresis, y diaeresis (Noel, naive, L'Hay). The diaeresis is the fifth and last European vowel diacritic, and three of its letters were undrawn. Drawing them completes the taxonomy.
think Reused the ASCII-art template from font5x7_tilde: same coverage_from_art, build_atlas, ink_count, row_band_ink shape. The diaeresis mark is the same two-dot mark the German umlaut carries (row 0 `.#.#.`, row 1 blank), over the circumflex e/i bodies and the lowercase y in rows 2-6.
think Designed three toothed placement guards distinguishing the diaeresis from every other lean: top-row ink == 2 (exactly two dots), center-column ink == 0 (the gap that parts them), second-mark-row ink == 0 (a single row of dots, where circumflex and tilde span two). Each its own bounded reader, no compound assert.
think Added a family-consistency crux beyond the round-trip: proved each diaeresis top row byte-identical to the German a umlaut's own top row (imported font5x7_german, built its atlas, compared column by column), so the accent family is one consistent hand rather than two that happen to look alike.
obs GREEN on the first metal run, no red: 3 diaeresis vowels U+00EB,U+00EF,U+00FF round-trip byte-identical, present, distinct, legible (ink 10..16 of 35), every mark two parted dots on one row and byte-identical to the German umlaut's. tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, both files plain 7-bit ASCII though the glyphs cover a non-ASCII range (numeric codepoint literals, the ascii-first font-table exception).
obs Docs-sync ratchet, not a sweep: image/README.md accreted the diaeresis corpus into the accented-Latin family entry, naming the fifth lean and the gap it fills, and added _diaeresis to the witness-sibling list. Did not claim it into the unifying font5x7_accented (a later merge round can gather the fifth lean); an honest sibling addition.
obs Rota this lap (d27, item 27) deep-read recursion-prompts/README.md -- the balance-compass charter: every prompt rewards something, and the craft keeps the reward pointed at finished, proven, bounded work. This lap is one such -- a single whole corpus, proven on metal, sent as its own signed round, Radiant prose swept before the send.
