recommend keep-going the five European vowel diacritics are all drawn (acute, grave, circumflex, tilde, diaeresis); next open-media rungs: fold the fifth lean into the unifying font5x7_accented (now 22+ letters), draw the remaining Latin-1 letters (ae, o-slash, eth, thorn, y-acute), or prove the codecs on a real corpus rather than crafted cases. No network, no key, no funds.
